\title{Competing Risks Task Generator}
\description{
A \link[mlr3:TaskGenerator]{mlr3::TaskGenerator} for simulating right-censored competing risks tasks
with numerical baseline covariates.

Uses \code{\link[=sim_cmprsk]{sim_cmprsk()}} to generate event times and causes from cause-specific
Weibull proportional hazards, with independent right-censoring.
The default \code{shape = 1} corresponds to constant cause-specific hazards
(exponential event times), while other values allow increasing or
decreasing hazards over time.

See \code{sim_cmprsk()} for the underlying statistical model, parameter
definitions, and defaults.
}
\details{
The generated \link{TaskCompRisks} contains the observed \code{time}, \code{event}, and
numerical features \code{x1}, ..., \code{xp}. Event codes are integers, with \code{0}
indicating censoring and \code{1}, ..., \code{n_causes} identifying competing causes.

Generation fails if any requested cause is absent among the observed events.
Event and censoring proportions may differ from their specified targets due
to sampling variability and covariate effects; see \code{\link[=sim_cmprsk]{sim_cmprsk()}} for details.

Use \code{\link[=set.seed]{set.seed()}} before \verb{$generate()} for reproducibility.
}
